{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/43788-a-story-of-a-completed-mummy-chronicle-sands-of-judgement","id":43788,"title":"A story of a completed Mummy Chronicle - Sands of Judgement","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-06T16:34:41-08:00","id":43788,"title":"A story of a completed Mummy Chronicle - Sands of Judgement","content":"I just wanted to share how my first campaign went. All but one guy is a long long term veteran of the CWoD and all were very new to NWoD. I was sucked into this game via Kickstarter when I was looking at what other things OP was up to. <br /> <br /> Firstly, I have an Obsidian Portal Page. It is here <a href=\"https://sands-of-judgement.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://sands-of-judgement.obsidianportal.com/</a>. Feel free to look over the PCs. We stopped updating it two sessions from the last as only I (the ST) used it and things were tightening up. Mechanic were loose and relics were over powered as we were figuring it out. I decided this was a time to go with yes. more yes. more more yes. It actually in the end went really well.<br /> <br /> The idea is I wanted to give the players a short series of 5-7 sessions to play through being epicly powerful. I also wanted to allow them to have an opportunity to merge the setting with a shared favorite setting.<br /> <br /> There were a number of events, like going to the IT department to find Benjamin, the IT manager for mocking them on their laptop. Or power playing the company their cult runs, etc. I am glossing over these as they were more flavor than storyline.<br /> <br /> The game started with their cult waking all 4 mummies while the tomb was under siege. Split assaults led to garou being speared by flagpoles telekinetically thrown, onces being disemboweled and even one mummy boxing three Garou punching out knee caps and such. They learn about the world and find their cult is being undermined by vampires. They address the issues with the werewolves and find out the werewolves thought the tower was a den of vampires. Then they learn the city is cut off and the sothic turn did not happen. They do research and end up fighting horrible shadow monsters which are remnants of something non-duat they sealed away in the time of Irem. They meet a shadowy mortal who was childlike (to a mummy anyway) who explained these are cropping up everywhere. They find out the Vampires had framed them to the werewolves and possibly others, thus the assault. Time to kick down the door.<br /> <br /> First though...one mummy decides to drop a comet on major vampire holdings in the city (these guys were not about subtlty). Then they got information about a meeting of the vampires. They roll in kick down the door and issue a decree to the Prince that he will be punished. Violence ensues which leads to a fighting pursuit in the sewers of the city. The mummies are mostly separated. One, a more mystic mummy, almost gets destroyed having to sacrifice a sekhem to refill willpower or else the Gangrel Primogen would have won. In the end the priomgen for the Brujan, Gangrel and the Sheriff are all cut down. Two mummies find a pit tainted with the shadow and they have a sit down with visions of their judges. One mummy corners and strikes a pact with the Nosferatu who states that his people think there are darker things and more ancient things in the area.<br /> <br /> After this they start to learn more of the issue with the stars not being in the sky thanks to them growing a mini-cult of Astronomancers. This leads them to set up a search on relics of various types they thought would help them. This lead them to an art auction with a Golden Scarab (3 feet diameter) with a broken leg. Oddly enough the various Secret Service like security guards seemed to know what they were and could spot them. Here they meet someone who tries to enlist them to work for the shadow. He was the diplomat from the age of Irem who made the same offer then. They restrained themselves however and waited. After locking the place up, they found the security system at night was a thousand hungry ghosts. They became embroiled in a fight with a bunch of shadows, the ghosts, themselves and later a wizard of immense power. They speed off leaving the combat mongers there cutting the shadow man down and eventually coming to terms with the wizard who they learn, is Harry Dresden from the Dresden Files. <br /> <br /> NOTE! If you have not read Cold Days and want to be surprised, do not read further.<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> Dresden takes the character to McAnally's where they have a one on one about whats going on. They soul gaze which shows the mummy Dresden is a bit special. Dresden gives him a card and time to meet him on the docks if they want to help. The mummies converse and find the Astronomancers have devised a method to punch through a caul which is covering sothis. The mummies then try to hunt down Dresden, going to his old office and then his old shell of an apartment where they find his cat sleeping. It refuses to leave even though they seem to like him. Dresden shows up having picked up he was being followed and proceeds, with the help of Bob, to explain what is happening. They all agree and go to Demonreach. Dresden takes them into the Prison and they discuss the ritual to fix the scarab (extended skill challenges with sekhem rank sacrifice). Ritual works while the shadow beasts are swarming to the island. Then time slows and the Mummies meet Demonreach who is actually a Judge cut off from the 42 who is serving as an inter-dimensional gaoler for things that should not be. They get this out of him but he is unable to speak directly about his task, what he was, or the judges themselves. He shows them to the place where they can use The Scarab (referred to by Bob as a 'Lock') and are able to fight down a manifestation of the shadow and seal the caves. <br /> <br /> Sothis becomes visible and mummies begin to awaken, and Chicago is no longer locked. Demonreach rewards them by restoring sekhem to them and restoring them to their correct deathless state. The mummies big storyline wise also join the accords.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It lasted 6 sessions and the players seemed to enjoy themselves.It was meant to be pulpy, tongue in cheek, and a minor nod to the fun that could be had by being 'Princes'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1559-cryocube","name":"cryocube","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}